  "description": "Codex: Orks (11e) army rule DA BOSS (WP-O34): 'At the start of the battle round, if a model with this ability is your WARLORD, gain 1CP.' Fixture ork11e_o34_active (P1 Orks, the Warboss is the WARLORD and carries Da Boss, vs P2 Custodes; battle round 2, P1 Command phase; P1 has the first turn). Loading into the round's first Command phase is the start of battle round 2: the Orks gain the core Command-phase CP AND the Da Boss CP (6 -> 8), the Game Log names it, and the Custodes (no Da Boss) gain only the core CP. The turn is then played out (phase ends dispatched; the Custodes are pushed 12\" back in setup so nothing is engaged). At the start of the Custodes' Command phase the Orks are offered WAR CRY in a rule window ('the Command phase', not 'your') — a real click on Decline closes it. Round 3 starts in the Orks' next Command phase: Da Boss grants exactly one more CP (with the core CP: +2), recorded for round 3.",
